      "obligation": "refuter:7:1",
      "id": "cor-evaluation-is-monic-and-coevaluation-is-epic-for-nonzero-objects",
      "location": "title",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "The title asserts the opposite directions from the item’s Statement. In $\\mathbf{Vect}^{\\mathrm{fd}}_k$ with $X=k^2$, $\\operatorname{ev}_X:X^*\\otimes X\\to k$ is surjective with a 3-dimensional kernel, while $\\operatorname{coev}_X:k\\to X\\otimes X^*$ is injective with 1-dimensional image in a 4-dimensional target. Thus evaluation is not monic and coevaluation is not epic.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "835c891feaeaab07dc58f3ff5d6257c6a380371ef1580e6504f86693f26470ba"
    },
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:7:2",
      "id": "cor-evaluation-is-monic-and-coevaluation-is-epic-for-nonzero-objects",
      "location": "Statement / source reference",
      "defect": "citation-inaccurate",
      "evidence": "The front matter cites EGNO, Corollary 4.3.9. Its text says: “the evaluation morphisms are monomorphisms and the coevaluation morphisms are epimorphisms,” whereas this item’s Statement asserts evaluation epic and coevaluation monic under the same left-dual types $X^\\vee\\otimes X\\to\\mathbf1$ and $\\mathbf1\\to X\\otimes X^\\vee$. The cited corollary therefore does not license the written directions.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "835c891feaeaab07dc58f3ff5d6257c6a380371ef1580e6504f86693f26470ba"
    },
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:7:3",
      "id": "cor-evaluation-is-monic-and-coevaluation-is-epic-for-nonzero-objects",
      "location": "Proof step 2.1",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "Dualizing $\\operatorname{ev}_X:X^\\vee\\otimes X\\to\\mathbf1$ by the chosen left-dual functor yields a map $\\mathbf1^\\vee\\to(X^\\vee\\otimes X)^\\vee\\cong X^\\vee\\otimes X^{\\vee\\vee}$, namely the coevaluation associated to $X^\\vee$, not $\\operatorname{coev}_X:\\mathbf1\\to X\\otimes X^\\vee$. Identifying these would require an unprovided $X\\cong X^{\\vee\\vee}$ coherence; [F2] only gives exactness.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "835c891feaeaab07dc58f3ff5d6257c6a380371ef1580e6504f86693f26470ba"
    },
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:7:4",
      "id": "rem-tensor-category-terminology-is-source-dependent",
      "location": "Remark",
      "defect": "citation-inaccurate",
      "evidence": "The cited EGNO Remark 4.2.6 says that exactness and faithfulness for a “(quasi)tensor functor” are imposed only in that book and may be omitted elsewhere. It does not discuss whether rigid $k$-linear abelian monoidal categories are called tensor categories, nor the scalar-unit convention asserted by this remark.",
